## N7 — three ownerless routes added to §6 (CORRECTION 11)

All three reviewer line ranges verified exact:

1. **`switchBindingLines` (`SwiftExpr.hx:5486-5490`)** — verified lines;
   delegates to `switchExpression` (:5523) → `switchReturn(sw, 1)` (:5524),
   whose arm check (:5639-5642) consults only `currentReturnType`. The
   binding's own destination is never consulted; if `currentReturnType` is not
   a read-only array, no consultation happens at all. Recorded precisely: the
   reviewer said "no owner"; the producer IS reached, but only with the wrong
   destination.
2. **`tryReturnLines` (`SwiftExpr.hx:5251`)** — exact. Value-form try-region
   returns: body (:5261) and handler (:5273) values come from
   `blockValueLines`; the emitted returns (:5269, :5282) bypass the :811
   dispatch (tryReturnLines is dispatched TO at :798-799 instead of :811).
   Genuinely lacks boundary consultation.
3. **try-region block tail `blockValueLines` (`SwiftExpr.hx:5160-5169`),
   specifically `:5168`** — exact. `expr(parts.value)`; `expr` (:1841)
   contains no boundary reference anywhere on its path. I enumerated every
   boundary-reference site in SwiftExpr.hx (:305, :743-746, :811, :1212,
   :1929, :2534-2535, :2566-2567, :2578-2614, :2627-2628, :2642-2643,
   :2672-2674, :2689, :2721, :2806-2807, :3304, :4720, :4760, :4863,
   :5641-5642, :6173) — none inside `expr`.

This required refining CORRECTION 3 in §4: its claim "try-body returns cross
the funnel via :811, so block/try tail is NOT untraced" is only true for
STATEMENT-form returns. That line now carries a PARTIALLY WRONG pointer to
CORRECTION 11, and the closing "So switch and try DO reach the single
producer" sentence now says "for try, only STATEMENT-form returns do". No
historical text was silently rewritten.

